account-note = Register an app at developer.spotify.com and give its client ID here, with http://127.0.0.1:43879/spotify among the app's redirect URIs. The sign-in happens in your browser and only a refresh token is kept, in the settings file. Spotify lets an app in development mode read only the playlists the account owns or collaborates on, so a playlist it merely follows is read from its public page: the first hundred songs at most, and not at all where it is private.
signed-in-note = Follow keeps the liked songs and every playlist in step, each a playlist here, read again every six hours; Move copies them once and follows nothing. A song the library lacks is wanted, found by its ISRC or a strict search, and one neither names is left out.
offline = Spotify is signed in to only while Online is on
no-client = Give the client ID of your Spotify app first
signed-in = Signed in to Spotify
no-account = Sign in to Spotify again: it no longer knows this account
the-sign-in-could-not-listen = The sign-in could not listen for its answer: is another sign-in open?
the-spotify-sign-in-was-not = The Spotify sign-in was not approved in time
spotify-was-told-not-to-sign = Spotify was told not to sign in
spotify-refused-the-sign-in-is = Spotify refused the sign-in: is the redirect listed on the app?
spotify-could-not-be-reached-to = Spotify could not be reached to sign in
the-client-id-of-your-app = The client ID of your app, then press enter
no-spotify-app-is-named-no = No Spotify app is named: no account is offered or asked
kept-for-signing-in-to-spotify = Kept for signing in to Spotify
signed-out-of-spotify-the-playlists = Signed out of Spotify: the playlists keep their rows and no longer follow it
let-the-account-go = let the account go
client-id = Client ID
